    "updated_at": "2026-11-20T10:47:59Z",
    "body": "fix on issue/2936-chamfer-leaning-wall · PR #2940 · pinned by `machining2d::chamfer_ride::tests::a_wall_leaning_in_the_frame_is_not_a_modelled_chamfer`, `machining2d::chamfer_ride::tests::a_moved_outline_with_one_side_bevelled_still_refuses` and `framed_stock_chamfer_live_refusal_keeps_hint_without_local_move_number` · merges when reviewed\n\nThe reason, as the issue asks:\n\n- The fixture loop is not partly chamfered. The fixture is a plain box stock under a frame tilted 10 degrees.\n- In that frame the top section is the corner section moved 0.176 mm (`1 mm * tan(10 deg)`) in Y. No edge carries a chamfer.\n- The check of #2894 (`partly_bevelled`) read the moved sides as bevelled and the other sides as sharp. That is a defect in the check, not in the fixture.\n- The fix is in the check. A top loop that is its wall loop moved whole is not read as bevelled. The fixture does not change.\n- The refusal of #2887 holds for a loop with a bevel on one side. Two unit tests and the two tests of `chamfer_partly_bevelled` confirm it.\n\nThe priority label is not changed. The maintainer decides if this is `P1` by the last paragraph of the issue body.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
